node_modules/
*.log
.env
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local Claude Code state — a dev artifact, not part of the plugin.
# marketplace.json uses "source": "./", so the repo root IS the plugin payload and
# everything tracked here is copied into every user's plugin cache on install.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Slash commands ARE tracked, and this line is what makes that true on the author's machine.
# A global core.excludesFile there ignores `.claude/commands/` outright, which would silently
# drop every command from the repo — present locally, absent in every clone, with no error.
# A repo .gitignore outranks the global one, and the negation must name the directory because
# a file cannot be re-included while its parent directory is excluded.
!.claude/commands/

# MCPB staging and the packed bundle. build/ is a throwaway staging tree; the .mcpb is a
# release artifact that GitHub Actions produces and attaches to a Release, never a tracked file.
build/
*.mcpb

# dist/ is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# PLUGIN-PRD P-09: the server ships as built JavaScript committed to the repo and is
# started as `node ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/dist/index.js` from .mcp.json. Adding dist/ here
# would ship a plugin whose MCP server never starts, and the harness reports that as the
# tools simply being absent (PC-02, "what the user sees when something is wrong").
#
# Keeping dist/ honest against src/ is open question PQ-06.
